# M5 — Back office: status

Updated: 2026-11-21 · App: Mieruka · Team: Zero-Ichi

## Decisions

- M5 is reserved for the back office: the administrative side where staff monitor every device, user, usage figure and credit.
- The STEG aggregated view (k-mod 07) becomes one tab of the back office later, keeping the 10-household minimum.
- User management moves to the new module M10 (login with Google through Clerk or FastAPI; choice still open). Until then the back office uses Django admin staff accounts.

## Current state

- Django app `m5` is registered in `config/settings.py` and routed at `/m5/`.
- Staff-only pages: overview, devices, users, user detail, alerts and credits (`m5/views.py`, `templates/m5/`).
- Data comes from the M2 models; `uv run manage.py seed_demo --reset` fills them with simulated households, adapters, readings, alerts and credits.
- Charts are server-rendered SVG, so the pages work in the Android app without JavaScript.
- Read-only for now: no actions (resolve alert, re-pair adapter, adjust credits) yet.
- Tests: `m5/tests.py` (access, rendering, filters, kWh calculation).

